      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Fremont, Elkhorn & Missouri Valley Railroad reached Oakdale in 1879, the town grew to 32 businesses and dwellings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.antelopecountymuseum.org/towns/oakdale"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Main Street hosts the Lois Johnson Memorial Library, the Church of Christ, and the village offices in the former First United Bank building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
